 (ΔShares ≤ 0)","passed":1,"detail":"未大幅增發新股割韭菜"},{"id":8,"category":"營運效率","desc":"毛利率擴張 (ΔMargin > 0)","passed":0,"detail":"產品定價權增強，毛利結構健康"},{"id":9,"category":"營運效率","desc":"資產週轉率提升 (ΔTurnover > 0)","passed":0,"detail":"每單位資產產出效益改善"}],"fair_val":146.06,"default_fair_val":146.06,"premium_pct":-82.3,"is_undervalued":true,"pe_trailing":16.3,"pe_forward":14.3,"pb_trailing":1.1,"pb_forward":1,"div_yield":4.2,"ps_ratio":1.9,"fcf_to_ev":2.59,"fcf_to_mcap":13.22,"liab_to_assets":61.1,"cash_to_assets":32.4,"current_ratio":1.14,"roe":6.6,"roa":2,"moat":{"ticker":"JD","period":"2026Q2","m1_brand_pricing":{"score":6,"comment_zh":"京東在中國電商市場建立了強大的品牌聲譽，尤其在 3C 產品和家電領域。其「自營+第三方」模式，結合對物流和售後服務的嚴格把控，形成了差異化的競爭優勢。然而，面對拼多多等低價競爭者以及直播電商的崛起，其品牌溢價能力面臨挑戰，尤其是在非標品類。品牌忠誠度雖高，但價格敏感度也是影響定價權的重要因素。","comment_en":"JD.com has cultivated a strong brand reputation in China's e-commerce landscape, particularly in 3C products and home appliances. Its 'direct sales + third-party' model, coupled with stringent control over logistics and after-sales service, creates a differentiated competitive advantage. However, facing low-price competitors like Pinduoduo and the rise of live-streaming e-commerce, its brand premium power is challenged, especially in non-standard product categories. While brand loyalty is high, price sensitivity remains a significant factor influencing pricing power."},"m2_patents_regulatory":{"score":1,"comment_zh":"京東作為一家電商平台，其核心競爭力不在於專利技術，而是運營效率和供應鏈管理。雖然在物流技術、無人機配送等方面有所投入，但這些並非構成嚴格的專利壁壘。監管環境對中國互聯網平台影響較大，雖然京東相對較少受到反壟斷調查的直接衝擊，但整體監管趨嚴仍是潛在風險，而非護城河。","comment_en":"As an e-commerce platform, JD.com's core competitiveness lies not in patented technology but in operational efficiency and supply chain management. While investments have been made in logistics technology and drone delivery, these do not constitute strict patent barriers. The regulatory environment significantly impacts Chinese internet platforms. Although JD has faced less direct impact from antitrust investigations compared to some peers, overall tightening regulations remain a potential risk rather than a moat."},"m3_high_switching_costs":{"score":5,"comment_zh":"京東的轉換成本相對中等。對於習慣了其高效物流、可靠售後和豐富商品選擇的用戶而言，轉換到其他平台可能意味著犧牲便利性和信任度。然而，中國電商市場競爭激烈，用戶對價格和促銷活動較為敏感，這降低了轉換成本。尤其是對於非核心品類的購買，用戶轉換的門檻較低。","comment_en":"JD.com's switching costs are moderate. For users accustomed to its efficient logistics, reliable after-sales service, and wide product selection, switching to other platforms might mean sacrificing convenience and trust. However, the fierce competition in China's e-commerce market makes users sensitive to prices and promotions, thereby lowering switching costs. Especially for purchases in non-core categories, the barrier to switching is relatively low."},"m4_network_effects":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"京東的網絡效應體現在其龐大的用戶基礎和活躍的商家生態。更多的消費者吸引更多的商家入駐，提供更多樣化的商品和服務；更多的商家和商品又反過來吸引更多消費者。其自營物流網絡也加強了這種網絡效應，形成了從供應鏈到終端用戶的閉環。然而，與純粹的社交或交易平台相比，其網絡效應的強度略有不同。","comment_en":"JD.com's network effects are evident in its vast user base and active merchant ecosystem. More consumers attract more merchants, offering a wider variety of goods and services, which in turn attracts more consumers. Its proprietary logistics network further strengthens these network effects, creating a closed loop from the supply chain to the end-user. However, compared to purely social or transactional platforms, the intensity of its network effects differs slightly."},"m5_cost_advantage_scale":{"score":8,"comment_zh":"京東憑藉其巨大的交易量和高效的自營物流網絡，實現了顯著的規模經濟。這使其在採購、倉儲、配送和客服方面擁有成本優勢。其龐大的基礎設施和技術投入，能夠攤薄固定成本，提供比小型競爭對手更低的運營成本。這種成本優勢是其在價格競爭中保持有利地位的關鍵。","comment_en":"Leveraging its massive transaction volume and efficient in-house logistics network, JD.com achieves significant economies of scale. This provides cost advantages in procurement, warehousing, delivery, and customer service. Its extensive infrastructure and technological investments allow for the amortization of fixed costs, offering lower operating expenses than smaller competitors. This cost advantage is crucial for maintaining a favorable position in price competition."},"m6_unique_geography_assets":{"score":3,"comment_zh":"京東的優勢在於其廣泛的中國市場覆蓋，尤其是在二三線城市及以下的滲透率。其物流網絡深入中國腹地，這是許多國際或區域性競爭對手難以複製的。然而，這更多是運營能力的體現，而非傳統意義上獨特的地理資產壁壘。中國市場本身競爭激烈，地理優勢的獨特性相對有限。","comment_en":"JD.com's strength lies in its extensive coverage of the Chinese market, particularly its penetration in lower-tier cities and below. Its logistics network reaches deep into China's heartland, which is difficult for many international or regional competitors to replicate. However, this is more a reflection of operational capability than a traditional unique geographical asset barrier. The Chinese market itself is highly competitive, limiting the uniqueness of its geographical advantage."},"m7_operational_efficiency":{"score":9,"comment_zh":"京東的運營效率是其核心競爭力之一。其自建的物流體系，包括倉儲、配送和最后一公里服務，效率極高，能夠提供快速可靠的交付體驗。通過數據分析和技術應用，持續優化庫存管理、訂單處理和路線規劃。這種卓越的運營能力構成了強大的護城河，尤其是在對時效性要求高的市場。","comment_en":"JD.com's operational efficiency is one of its core competitive strengths. Its self-built logistics system, encompassing warehousing, distribution, and last-mile delivery, is highly efficient, enabling fast and reliable delivery experiences. Through data analytics and technological applications, it continuously optimizes inventory management, order processing, and route planning. This superior operational capability forms a strong moat, especially in markets where timeliness is critical."},"m8_capital_allocation":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"京東近年來在資本配置上展現出更為審慎的態度，聚焦核心電商業務和物流基礎設施的投入，並剝離非核心業務（如京東雲）。其充足的現金儲備和健康的資產負債表為其提供了戰略靈活性。儘管過去在多元化拓展上有所嘗試，但目前更側重於提升主業的盈利能力和效率，這符合價值投資的原則。","comment_en":"In recent years, JD.com has demonstrated a more prudent approach to capital allocation, focusing investments on core e-commerce operations and logistics infrastructure while divesting non-core businesses (e.g., JD Cloud). Its ample cash reserves and healthy balance sheet provide strategic flexibility. Although diversification attempts were made in the past, the current focus is on enhancing the profitability and efficiency of its main business, aligning with value investing principles."},"m9_customer_retention":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"京東通過其優質的服務、可靠的產品質量以及會員計劃（如京東PLUS）來維持客戶忠誠度。PLUS會員提供運費補貼、折扣券和專屬服務，有效提升了用戶黏性。結合其強大的物流網絡和完善的售後服務，為用戶提供了持續的良好體驗，從而提高了客戶留存率。然而，面對激烈的市場競爭，持續的客戶維護仍是關鍵。","comment_en":"JD.com maintains customer loyalty through its high-quality services, reliable product quality, and membership programs like JD PLUS. PLUS members receive shipping subsidies, discount coupons, and exclusive services, effectively enhancing user stickiness. Combined with its robust logistics network and comprehensive after-sales support, it provides a consistently positive user experience, thereby improving customer retention rates. However, continuous customer engagement remains key amidst intense market competition."},"m10_durability":{"score":6,"comment_zh":"京東的商業模式具有一定的持久性，尤其是在其核心的自營電商和物流領域。中國消費者對線上購物的依賴性持續增長，為京東提供了穩定的市場基礎。然而，電商行業變化迅速，技術革新（如AI、直播帶貨）和新興競爭者不斷湧現，對其傳統模式構成潛在的顛覆性威脅。其持久性取決於持續的創新和適應能力。","comment_en":"JD.com's business model possesses a degree of durability, especially in its core direct sales e-commerce and logistics segments. The increasing reliance of Chinese consumers on online shopping provides a stable market base for JD. However, the e-commerce industry is rapidly evolving, with technological innovations (like AI, live-streaming commerce) and emerging competitors posing potential disruptive threats to its traditional model. Its durability depends on continuous innovation and adaptability."},"overall_moat_verdict_zh":"京東的護城河主要體現在其卓越的運營效率和規模經濟所帶來的成本優勢，特別是其自建的龐大物流網絡，構成了難以被快速複製的競爭壁壘。這使其在中國電商市場中，尤其是在一二線城市及家電、3C等標品領域，具有類似「收費橋」的穩定性。品牌聲譽和客戶忠誠度（透過PLUS會員體現）也提供了一定支撐。然而，面對拼多多等低價競爭者以及直播電商等新興模式的挑戰，其定價權和網絡效應的絕對優勢受到侵蝕。監管風險和行業快速變化的特性，限制了其護城河的絕對強度，使其更偏向於一個高效運營的商品型企業，而非擁有強大特許經營權的公司。","overall_moat_verdict_en":"JD.com's moat primarily lies in its exceptional operational efficiency and the cost advantages derived from economies of scale, particularly its self-built, extensive logistics network, which forms a difficult-to-replicate competitive barrier. This provides stability, akin to a 'toll bridge,' in the Chinese e-commerce market, especially in first and second-tier cities and for standard goods like appliances and 3C products. Brand reputation and customer loyalty (evidenced by PLUS membership) also offer support. However, challenges from low-price competitors like Pinduoduo and emerging models like live-streaming commerce erode its pricing power and absolute network effect advantages. Regulatory risks and the industry's rapid evolution limit the absolute strength of its moat, positioning it more as an efficiently operated 'commodity-like' business rather than a company with strong franchise power.","evidenceHash":"769a65ab9ab6ac666ee68a986587bb34a1408b266058bd50b66c05a1ef7a8387","assessmentPolicy":"us-buffett-moat-v3"},"ratingSources":{"moat":{"reason":null},"fScore":{"score":5,"checkedAt":null},"zScore":{"asOfDate":"2025-12-31","period":"FY 2025","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":"z","zone":"grey","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"CNY","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-27T16:12:46.364Z","evidenceHash":"a3d1ea8d44291e9d11728e4b735dcf6585ecaf401781a70cef1427b734b606cc"},"mScore":{"asOfDate":"2025-12-31","period":"FY 2025","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":null,"zone":"clean","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"CNY","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-27T16:12:46.364Z","evidenceHash":"a3d1ea8d44291e9d11728e4b735dcf6585ecaf401781a70cef1427b734b606cc"}},"fin_valuation":{"is_financial":false},"image":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/JD.png","logo":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/JD.png","website":"https://global.jd.com","ceo":"Ran Xu","full_time_employees":"900000","description":"JD.com, Inc. is a prominent technology and service provider based in the People's Republic of China, distinguished by its robust, supply chain-centric operations. The company's retail segment offers a comprehensive array of products. This includes computing devices, communication equipment, and various consumer electronics, alongside a broad selection of home appliances. Beyond these, JD.com provides an extensive general merchandise category, covering everything from groceries (food, beverages, fresh produce) and daily essentials (baby and maternity items, furniture, household goods, personal care, cosmetics, pharmaceuticals, health products) to specialized goods (industrial products, books, automotive accessories, apparel, footwear, bags, and jewelry). Additionally, the firm extends a variety of services, such as hosting an online marketplace for external vendors, delivering marketing solutions, providing omni-channel retail strategies for both consumers and traditional brick-and-mortar stores, and offering online healthcare services. JD.com also plays a significant role in infrastructure, developing, owning, and managing its own logistics facilities and other real estate assets. These capabilities not only support its internal operations but also serve third parties through asset management services, an integrated service platform, and the leasing and management of storage facilities. Beyond consumer and retail services, the company offers integrated industry solutions encompassing data analytics, technology, business operations, and user management, all designed to facilitate the digital transformation of various enterprises and institutions. It also delivers advanced, technology-driven supply chain and logistics services. Incorporated in 2006, JD.com, Inc. is headquartered in Beijing, the People's Republic of China. The company was formerly known as 360buy Jingdong Inc. until it officially changed its name to JD.com, Inc. in January 2014.","description_en":"JD.com, Inc. is a prominent technology and service provider based in the People's Republic of China, distinguished by its robust, supply chain-centric operations. The company's retail segment offers a comprehensive array of products. This includes computing devices, communication equipment, and various consumer electronics, alongside a broad selection of home appliances. Beyond these, JD.com provides an extensive general merchandise category, covering everything from groceries (food, beverages, fresh produce) and daily essentials (baby and maternity items, furniture, household goods, personal care, cosmetics, pharmaceuticals, health products) to specialized goods (industrial products, books, automotive accessories, apparel, footwear, bags, and jewelry). Additionally, the firm extends a variety of services, such as hosting an online marketplace for external vendors, delivering marketing solutions, providing omni-channel retail strategies for both consumers and traditional brick-and-mortar stores, and offering online healthcare services. JD.com also plays a significant role in infrastructure, developing, owning, and managing its own logistics facilities and other real estate assets. These capabilities not only support its internal operations but also serve third parties through asset management services, an integrated service platform, and the leasing and management of storage facilities. Beyond consumer and retail services, the company offers integrated industry solutions encompassing data analytics, technology, business operations, and user management, all designed to facilitate the digital transformation of various enterprises and institutions. It also delivers advanced, technology-driven supply chain and logistics services. Incorporated in 2006, JD.com, Inc. is headquartered in Beijing, the People's Republic of China. The company was formerly known as 360buy Jingdong Inc. until it officially changed its name to JD.com, Inc. in January 2014.","description_zh":"**京東集團 (JD.com, Inc.) 業務營運概述**\n\n京東集團為中國領先的科技與服務提供者，以其強健的供應鏈為核心營運特色。公司零售業務涵蓋多元商品，包括電腦通訊、消費電子、家電等。此外，亦提供廣泛的日用百貨，從生鮮食品、日用品、母嬰用品、家居、美妝、藥品保健，到工業品、圖書、汽車配件、服飾鞋包、珠寶等應有盡有。\n\n京東亦提供多樣化服務，包含第三方賣家線上市集、行銷解決方案、全通路零售策略（涵蓋線上線下），以及線上醫療服務。公司積極佈局基礎設施，自建並營運物流設施與不動產，不僅支援自有業務，亦透過資產管理、整合服務平台及倉儲租賃等，為第三方提供服務。\n\n此外，京東亦提供整合性產業解決方案，包含數據分析、技術、營運及用戶管理，協助企業數位轉型。公司並提供先進的科技驅動供應鏈與物流服務。京東集團成立於2006年，總部位於北京。","address":"Building A, 20th Floor","city":"Beijing","state":"BE","zip":"101111","country":"CN","phone":"86 40 0606 5500","full_address":"Building A, 20th Floor, Beijing, BE 101111, CN","range_52w":"24.508-35.06","year_high":35.06,"year_low":24.508,"all_time_high":0,"all_time_low":24.508,"inst_ownership_pct":null,"insider_ownership_pct":null,"top_holders":[],"insider_trades":[{"date":"2026-09-23","name":"Li Carol Yun Yau","title":"director","is_buy":null,"action":"M-Exempt","shares":9329,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-09-23","name":"Li Carol Yun Yau","title":"director","is_buy":null,"action":"M-Exempt","shares":18658,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-08-17","name":"Yu Jennifer Ngar-Wing","title":"director","is_buy":null,"action":"M-Exempt","shares":6950,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-08-17","name":"Yu Jennifer Ngar-Wing","title":"director","is_buy":null,"action":"M-Exempt","shares":13900,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-08-17","name":"Ding Kun","title":"director","is_buy":null,"action":"M-Exempt","shares":6950,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-08-17","name":"Ding Kun","title":"director","is_buy":null,"action":"M-Exempt","shares":13900,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-07-06","name":"Shan Su","title":"officer: Chief Financial Officer","is_buy":null,"action":"M-Exempt","shares":1250,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-07-06","name":"Shan Su","title":"officer: Chief Financial Officer","is_buy":null,"action":"F-InKind","shares":574,"price":26.46,"total_val":0.02},{"date":"2026-07-06","name":"Shan Su","title":"officer: Chief Financial Officer","is_buy":null,"action":"M-Exempt","shares":2500,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-07-06","name":"Xu Ran","title":"director, officer: Chief Executive Officer","is_buy":null,"action":"M-Ex